  "text": {
    "status": "additional",
    "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><h2>MaP Endpoint Capability Statement</h2><table><tbody><tr><th>Responsible Organization / Service</th><td>DirectTrust Payload Testing Tool</td></tr><tr><th>Direct Address</th><td>mapFramework@Direct3.DirectTrust.org</td></tr><tr><th>Supported Use Case</th><td>cc-maternal-health-birth</td></tr><tr><th>FHIR Version</th><td>R4 (4.0.1)</td></tr><tr><th>Last Updated</th><td>2026-10-12</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Reusable Transaction Catalog Capability</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Transaction</th><th>Send</th><th>Receive</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>send-outpatient-visit-notification</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>send-admission-notification</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>send-birth-notification</td><td>No</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>send-discharge-notification</td><td>No</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>send-documents</td><td>No</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>query-for-documents</td><td>No</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>send-patient-update</td><td>No</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>send-workflow-status</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr></tbody></table><p>All eight catalog transactions are enumerated. Catalog membership is distinct from declared endpoint support: Send and Receive are asserted independently for each transaction. The current testing-endpoint declaration establishes receive support for send-outpatient-visit-notification and send-admission-notification, and establishes send-workflow-status in both directions; the remaining catalog entries are retained explicitly with unsupported directions until those endpoint capabilities are established.</p><h3>Metadata Packaging</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Representation</th><th>Send</th><th>Receive</th><th>Preferred</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Payload containing XDM Metadata</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Payload containing FHIR Metadata</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Correlated Response Packaging</h3><p>TX8 normally uses the same metadata packaging representation as the originating MaP transaction when that representation is supported for the response.</p><h3>Implementation Note</h3><p>The CapabilityStatement enumerates the complete Reusable Transaction Catalog. A false direction flag means that direction is not currently declared as supported by this endpoint; it does not remove the transaction from the catalog.</p></div>"
  },
